      "automation_source": "clawsweeper",
      "repair_reason": "- No automated repair is needed; the remaining action is maintainer review of merge order and the intended fail-closed behavior.; Cleared: No supply-chain, workflow, dependency, permission, or secret-handling concern was found; the diff narrows memory-exhaustion exposure by bounding external response reads. (sha=fbbab0d3ccf91d1019de88e16e040ac75ecad2e2)",
      "review_summary": "The PR bounds Discord webhook success-body parsing and Google/OpenRouter OAuth token response reads with shared provider HTTP readers while preserving Discord 204 no-body success.\n\nPR surface: Source +15. Total +15 across 3 files.\n\nReproducibility: yes. Current main has unbounded response.text()/response.json() reads in the touched success and error paths, and the PR body provides after-fix loopback terminal output for normal, oversized, malformed, and 204 cases; I did not run tests locally because this review is read-only.",
      "review_followup": "- No automated repair is needed; the remaining action is maintainer review of merge order and the intended fail-closed behavior.",
